.TH ZTOP 1 "November 2026" "zTop 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ztop \- a lightweight system monitor for macOS and Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ztop
[
.BI options
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ztop
is a lightweight system monitor that displays CPU, memory, disk, and network
usage in real time. It runs as a local agent that collects metrics and serves
them over a secure, paired connection; a client (the TUI) renders them.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.B agent
Run the zTop agent (the default when no subcommand is given).
.TP
.B hub
Run the zTop hub, which polls the agents named in
.B --agents
and serves their combined view.
.TP
.BI "connect " target
Drive the TUI from a remote agent or hub.
.TP
.B capture
Record this host's raw inputs as a fixture for collector tests.
.TP
.B replay
Render one TUI frame from a recorded fixture.
.SH AGENT OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-port " PORT"
The port to listen on (default: 7100).
.TP
.BI \-\-bind " ADDRESS"
The address to bind to (default: 127.0.0.1). Anything wider than loopback
requires
.B \-\-tls
, so no unauthenticated metrics ever leave the machine.
.TP
.B \-\-tls
Serve HTTPS with a self-signed certificate and require tokens.
.TP
.B \-\-pair
Show a pairing code a client can trade for a token.
.TP
.B \-\-allow\-control
Let paired tokens send signals and renice processes. Off by default.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-advertise
Skip the Bonjour advertisement that
.B \-\-tls
turns on.
.SH HUB OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-port " PORT"
The port to listen on (default: 7101).
.TP
.BI \-\-agents " FILE"
The agents to watch, as a JSON file of
.nf
{"agents":[{"name":"...","target":"...","pin":"...","token":"..."}]}
.fi
.TP
.BI \-\-db " FILE"
Where the history lives (SQLite); default under the state directory.
.TP
.BI \-\-bind " ADDRESS"
The address to bind to (default: 127.0.0.1).
.TP
.B \-\-pair
Print a pairing code so a client can pair with the hub.
.TP
.B \-\-tls
Serve HTTPS with a self-signed certificate and enforce tokens.
.SH CONNECT OPTIONS
.TP
.BI target
The agent or hub to connect to, e.g.
.BR 127.0.0.1:7100 .
.TP
.B \-\-tls
Connect over TLS, verifying the certificate against
.BR \-\-pin .
.TP
.BI \-\-pin " FINGERPRINT"
The certificate fingerprint, exactly as the agent printed it:
.BR SHA256:<64\ hex> .
.TP
.BI \-\-code " CODE"
The pairing code, traded once for a token and then saved under the state
directory for this host.
.TP
.B \-\-once
Read one sample, print a one-line summary, and exit: the non-interactive
client for scripts and CI pairing checks.
.SH FILES
.TP
.BI ~/.config/ztop/
State directory (tokens, hub history). Honors
.BR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME .
.SH EXAMPLES
Run the agent with TLS and pairing:
.PP
.nf
$ ztop agent \-\-tls \-\-pair
.fi
.PP
Pair a client and open the TUI:
.PP
.nf
$ ztop connect \-\-tls \-\-pin SHA256:... \-\-code ABCDEF 127.0.0.1:7100
.fi
.SH AUTHOR
zTop Maintainers <maintainers@ztop.dev>
